Z||000000||turbo86se||12-07-1999||12:37 PM||||<BR>Hello again,<BR>I found a supplier for the 5.25 inch Bazooka bass tubes that fit perfectly behind the seats on the Fiero. I found this supplier on ebay. I paid $99 for a brand-new pair of subs. Delivery was in four days! As far as I know SAS does not produce these any more. And the supplier has about 15 pairs left. LMK if anyone is interested in these. It's going to be while until I install these, my 86SE has the factory sub, and I don't know what I'm going to do with that set-up. Maybe I'll switch the factory set-up over to my 88 coupe, would that be too difficult?  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||12-08-1999||01:57 AM||||I just ordered a new sound system, for my Fiero, from Crutchfield. Let me know how the subwoofer instalation goes. I might be interested. Are they amplified or do they require an external amp? I also might be interested in your stock setup if it comes up for sale.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88 Fiero||12-08-1999||04:41 PM||||I already have a pair of SAS Bazooka tubes 5.25 behind my car seats...both driver and passenger side using the factory subwoofer controls and amp..although I have to add another amp for the second tubes.. I eliminated the factory subwoofer and it sounds better than factory...||||reg||1
